WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.315
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:09.199
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:15.948
Unit seven: Second Conditional (introduction). Today you will talk about imaginary situations in the present.

4
00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:18.889
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:23.147
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.983 --> 00:00:25.077
If I were.

7
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:29.070
If I were means a pattern to imagine being someone else.

8
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:31.532
If I were you, I would study.

9
00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:34.630
Your turn. Say: If I were.

10
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:38.433
If I were.

11
00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:39.883
Would.

12
00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:43.243
Would means used for imaginary results.

13
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.990
I would travel.

14
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.806
Your turn. Say: Would.

15
00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:51.436
Would.

16
00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:53.324
Hypothetical.

17
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:56.839
Hypothetical means imagined and not real.

18
00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.600
It is a hypothetical situation.

19
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:03.426
Your turn. Say: Hypothetical.

20
00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:07.430
Hypothetical.

21
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:09.451
Unreal present.

22
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:13.843
Unreal present means a present situation that is not true.

23
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:16.275
Being rich is unreal for me.

24
00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:19.756
Your turn. Say: Unreal present.

25
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.402
Unreal present.

26
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.105
Imagine.

27
00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:29.627
Imagine means to picture something in your mind.

28
00:01:30.217 --> 00:01:31.798
Imagine you are a bird.

29
00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:34.722
Your turn. Say: Imagine.

30
00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:38.637
Imagine.

31
00:01:39.383 --> 00:01:40.036
Wish.

32
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.502
Wish means to want something that is not true.

33
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:45.652
I wish I had more time.

34
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.566
Your turn. Say: Wish.

35
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.204
Wish.

36
00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:53.998
Not real.

37
00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:57.331
Not real means different from the facts.

38
00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:59.510
The story is not real.

39
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:02.781
Your turn. Say: Not real.

40
00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:06.762
Not real.

41
00:02:07.517 --> 00:02:08.529
Possibility.

42
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:12.027
Possibility means something that might be true.

43
00:02:12.617 --> 00:02:14.152
There is a possibility.

44
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.646
Your turn. Say: Possibility.

45
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.617
Possibility.

46
00:02:22.433 --> 00:02:26.514
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:30.929
Visal, write a second conditional about something you wish were different.

48
00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:43.272
If I had more free time, I would learn the piano. The second conditional is for imaginary situations: if + past simple, would + base verb.

49
00:02:44.383 --> 00:02:46.638
Is the past tense about the past?

50
00:02:47.750 --> 00:03:04.409
No. It is the unreal present. The past simple shows that the situation is not real. We say if I were, not if I was, for all persons in careful English: If I were you, I would study.

51
00:03:05.517 --> 00:03:07.760
How is it different from the first conditional?

52
00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:24.276
First is a real possibility: If I win, I will celebrate. Second is imaginary or unlikely: If I won, I would celebrate. The second shows we do not expect it.

53
00:03:25.433 --> 00:03:27.468
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:28.317 --> 00:03:33.880
Grammar focus: Second conditional: If plus past simple, would plus base verb.

55
00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:35.402
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:36.117 --> 00:03:39.115
If I had more free time, I would learn the piano.

57
00:03:40.017 --> 00:03:42.121
If I were you, I would study harder.

58
00:03:43.017 --> 00:03:45.492
If she won the prize, she would travel the world.

59
00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:55.996
Use if + past simple, would + base verb for imaginary or unlikely situations. Say if I were. The past tense is not about past time here.

60
00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.203
Be careful! Don't say: If I would have time, I would go.

61
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.782
Say: If I had time, I would go.

62
00:04:05.082 --> 00:04:07.220
Use the past simple in the if-clause.

63
00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.825
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:11.633 --> 00:04:12.681
Imagine If….

65
00:04:12.981 --> 00:04:15.538
If I had more free time, I would learn the piano.

66
00:04:16.533 --> 00:04:18.893
If I were you, I would study harder.

67
00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.585
If she won the prize, she would travel the world.

68
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:26.830
These situations are hypothetical, not real.

69
00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:30.042
Imagine how different life would be.

70
00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:35.181
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:36.017 --> 00:04:38.028
If I blank rich, I would travel.

72
00:04:38.328 --> 00:04:41.354
A, am. B, were. C, will be.

73
00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.493
The answer is B: were.

74
00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.313
She blank help if she knew.

75
00:04:49.613 --> 00:04:52.802
A, will. B, would. C, can.

76
00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:58.099
The answer is B: would.

77
00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.412
Which sentence is a second conditional?

78
00:05:01.712 --> 00:05:08.407
A, If it rains, we will stay.. B, If I won, I would celebrate.. C, If you heat ice, it melts..

79
00:05:11.967 --> 00:05:14.767
The answer is B: If I won, I would celebrate..

80
00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:17.638
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:17.938 --> 00:05:24.656
A, If I would have time, I would go.. B, If I had time, I would go.. C, If I have time, I would go..

82
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.768
The answer is B: If I had time, I would go..

83
00:05:31.917 --> 00:05:35.100
According to the reading, what does the writer imagine?

84
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:39.925
A, a different life. B, yesterday. C, a test.

85
00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:45.559
The answer is A: a different life.

86
00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:49.930
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:54.954
Write a second conditional sentence about something you wish were different.

88
00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.192
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:05.492 --> 00:06:18.352
If I lived near the sea, I would swim every morning. I live far from the beach, so this situation is imaginary. I use the past simple in the if-clause and would in the result.

90
00:06:18.652 --> 00:06:20.304
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:21.217 --> 00:06:27.921
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and second conditional: if plus past simple, would plus base verb.

92
00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:33.033
Today's value is imagination. Imagine new ideas for a better future.

93
00:06:33.333 --> 00:06:35.602
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:35.902 --> 00:06:38.740
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

